{"id": "EUVD-2026-91437", "enisaUuid": "00264f3e-59a0-3c05-aee2-2b5a495bcd73", "description": "Zebra before 6.1.0 contains an inefficient algorithmic complexity vulnerability in remaining_transaction_value that clones the entire block-level spent-UTXO map per transaction during contextual verification. Attackers can mine or seed the mempool with roughly 26,000 minimal single-input transactions in one block, stalling every validating node for over 52 seconds.", "datePublished": "2026-10-02T11:38:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T15:18:42", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ZcashFoundation/zebra/security/advisories/GHSA-4g24-549m-hp75", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zebra-before-6.1.0-quadratic-complexity-dos-via-block-transparent-value-check"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-104426", "GHSA-g338-vc6m-x872"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f3a7045d-9feb-326c-86d3-584c757a77aa", "product": {"name": "zebra", "vendor": {"name": "ZcashFoundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "03417074-35cf-33ef-bf13-ca377de102ae", "vendor": {"name": "ZcashFoundation"}}], "isExploited": false}